      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u0027Having Stub impl in static inner class and holding WeakReference of holding Context\u0027 is a coding pattern to avoid `Context` leak 100%. If Binder object is shared across the process and counterparty holds it, this stub reference would never be garbage collected. If it\u0027s the inner class or the same as `Context`, then `Context` would remain valid even after garbage collected.\n\nStrictly speaking, it wouldn\u0027t happen here because all happens in the same process. However, since I choose standard approach (AIDL) for Service and Activity communication (instead of calling each others APIs directly), Let me follow the recommended practice.",
      "parentUuid": "e52d215f_42491f1f",
